[[Dante Vale]] used Spidertouch to cling onto [[Ymir]] during the mission [[The Hammer of Thor]], making the giant [[Titans|Titan]] fall into a nearby canyon. {{Source|The Legacy of Thor|}} Inside a ship belonging to [[Atalanta|Atlanta]] sunk in the [[Stavropolous River]], Dante Vale used this spell once again to grab the [[Sword of Saint George]] from [[DeFoe]]'s hands, with which he was holding Sophie Casterwill hostage. {{Source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

In the outskirts of [[Vienna, Austria]], Dante Vale used Spidertouch with the help of [[Hyperstride]] to grab onto an [[The Organization|Organization]] helicopter trying to stop them from entering [[Klaus' bookshop|Klaus' Bookshop]]. With the spell's help, Dante is able to stay firmly gripped to the helicopter and invoke [[Metagolem]], bringing it down. {{Source|The Bookshop Hunter}}

At some point, [[LeBlanche]] used Spidertouch to restrain two [[Suits]]. {{Source|TCG:SAS-114|SAS-114}}

[[Lok Lambert]] used the spell to fight off a pair of thugs when looking for [[Den Fears]] in the streets of Venice, restraining one of them to a nearby log. {{Source|Boys Will Be Seekers}} It was later used by Lok to save himself from falling from a narrow bridge, part of the Trial of Courage inside the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{Source|Sophie on Trial}}

[[Guggenheim]] used this spell in conjunction with [[Ironhand]] to break apart a wooden plank from the ceiling of the [[Hamelin Cathedral]], falling onto several [[Gremlow]] Titans. {{Source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

Dante Vale and [[Den Fears]] both used an orange aura Spidertouch spell to restrain [[Shauna]] during a surprise attack inside the [[Phoenix Volcano]]. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}} Den later used the spell once again to stop [[Cherit]] from eating a loaf of bread Den wanted to eat during the team's rest at the [[Lambert house|Lambert House]]. {{Source|Back Home}}

