[[Lok Lambert]] used the spell to fight off a pair of thugs when looking for [[Den Fears]] in the streets of Venice, restraining one of them to a nearby log. {{Source|Boys Will Be Seekers}} It was later used by Lok to save himself from falling from a narrow bridge, part of the Trial of Courage inside the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{Source|Sophie on Trial}}

[[Guggenheim]] used this spell in conjunction with [[Ironhand]] to break apart a wooden plank from the ceiling of the [[Hamelin Cathedral]], falling onto several [[Gremlow]] Titans. {{Source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

Dante Vale and [[Den Fears]] both used an orange aura Spidertouch spell to restrain [[Shauna]] during a surprise attack inside the [[Phoenix Volcano]]. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}} Den later used the spell once again to stop [[Cherit]] from eating a loaf of bread Den wanted to eat during the team's rest at the [[Lambert house|Lambert House]]. {{Source|Back Home}}

== Trivia ==
* [[Lok Lambert]]'s use of Spidertouch in episode 36, "[[Boys Will Be Seekers]]" is an allusion to [[wikipedia:Spider-Man|Spider-Man]].
* In the TCG, [[SAS-024|SAS-024 - Zhalia Moon]] grants a bonus whenever she uses this spell.
* When Dante Vale and Den Fears use the spell in the episode "[[The Phoenix's Ashes]]", its aura is orange instead of the usual blue.

